<title>POLAND: BRE to issue first Polish bond warrants.</title>
<headline>BRE to issue first Polish bond warrants.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) will issue one-year American call warrants on Poland's 16-percent two-year bonds and 12-percent five-year bonds from next week, a bank official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This product is the first-ever derivative for an instrument of Polish capital market,&quot; Dariusz Gatarek, senior analyst at BRE's Treasury Department told Reuters.</p>
<p>The bank envisages demand for derivatives to grow rapidly on the Polish market in the near future.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
